<title>USA: May raises dividend, sets repurchase.</title>
<headline>May raises dividend, sets repurchase.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>May Department Stores Co said Wednesday it increased its quarterly dividend to $0.30 per share from $0.29, bringing the annual dividend to $1.20 a share from $1.16, effective with the March 15, 1997 payment for holders of record as of March 1.</p>
<p>In addition, the board said it authorized the company to repurchase up to $300 million of May shares.  This is in addition to the $600 million repurchase program that May announced in August 1996 and completed in January.  </p>
<p>The retailer said it expects to make the new purchases through open-market transactions.  Timing will depend on market conditions.</p>
<p>At February 1, 1997, May had 258.2 million fully diluted average shares and share equivalents outstanding.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
